//~ ErrorDupName:1 "conflicting definition"
// A submodule that declares nothing: the folder bare/ names it, and no 'mod'
// line restates the name. A declaration of the parent spelling 'bare' collides
// with it, and this module's half of that diagnostic has no declaration to be
// reported at, so it is reported at the first line of this file -- the file that
// makes bare/ a module, which is the nearest thing the module has to one. The
// annotation on line 1 is that half.

pub fn bareFn(n i64) i64 {
  n;
}
